\section*{Declaration of generative AI and AI-assisted technologies}

During the preparation of this work the authors used Claude Opus (model identifier claude-opus-5-5) through a multi-agent manuscript-writing workflow. Specifically, the tool was used for research assistance (the literature search, the screening of sources and their annotation), for drafting assistance (the outline and the first draft of the text), for the placement and captions of the figures, for checking citations against their sources, and for a simulated peer review of the draft. Revision assistance: [GAP: AI use category Revision assistance not confirmed]. Editing assistance: [GAP: AI use category Editing assistance not confirmed]. Research assistance, drafting assistance and peer review simulation outside this workflow: [GAP: AI use category Research assistance not confirmed] [GAP: AI use category Drafting assistance not confirmed] [GAP: AI use category Peer review simulation not confirmed]. Language models can produce incorrect statements and incorrect references, so their output has to be checked against the sources and the results of the study. [GAP: human oversight: which author reviewed which AI-assisted content, and at which stages]. The tool is not an author. The authors take full responsibility for the content of the published article.

Analysis: [GAP: AI use category Analysis assistance not confirmed]. The tool computed no number reported in this manuscript during its preparation. Every reported number was computed in the statistical analysis of the study.

\section*{Reproducibility statement}

The cohort definition, the inclusion and exclusion criteria, the models with their hyperparameters, and the evaluation are documented in the Method and Experiments sections. The declaration of generative AI use describes the AI assistance used to prepare the manuscript. The reported numbers come from the analysis of the study. Replication or extension of this work requires credentialed access to MIMIC-IV and MIMIC-IV-ECG under the PhysioNet data use agreement. The sampling of controls, the cross-validation folds and the initialisations of the networks are seeded. The code is available under the MIT licence at [GAP: repository URL or DOI].

